Now drawSky and background. Let's replace drawSky sun/cloud colors with map values and add map-specific extras. Current drawSky lines 475-525 (shifted). We'll replace entire function maybe.

Plan:
```
function drawSky(t){
 const map=currentMap||MAPS[0];
 ctx.fillStyle=skyGrad; fillRect...
 // sun position: rooftop .74/.22, harbor .78/.18, temple .68/.2
 const sunX...
 rays with withA(map.sun,.05)
 glow gradient: 0 withA(map.sun,.55), .5 map.glow, 1 transparent
 sun fill map.sun
 // stars alpha based decor: harbor .8, temple .5, rooftop .35
 // clouds color map-specific, alpha
 if temple: canopy? handled drawBackdrop.
